      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC0",
      "licenseUrl": "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en",
      "artist": "PlywoodPelican",
      "description": "This image was taken inside the Forsgate Conservatory of the Hong Kong Park, specifically Humid Plant House section. The waterfall spans the entire length of this section in a spiral path, that you can follow from the top to where it all eventually flows into the artificial lake at the bottom. Following the therapeutic rhythm and sight of the waterfall, you can see a wide variety of ferns, palms, bromeliads, carnivorous plants and jungle foliage plants from South Africa, Southeast Asia and America. These exhibits are arranged in zonal groups according to their places of origin. The air inside this section, and specially this part of the waterfall is revitalizingly clean. Growing up in a concrete jungle like Hong Kong, makes me cherish moments like these. You usually have to travel far to see greenery like that depicted in this image, and even further to breath in fresh clean air.",
